<title>GERMANY: German railmen oppose transport of nuclear waste.</title>
<headline>German railmen oppose transport of nuclear waste.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG, Germany 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German railworkers union GdED on Tuesday called for an end to the transport of nuclear waste by rail and said attacks on rail facilities by anti-nuclear protestors put railworkers' lives in danger.</p>
<p>In a resolution passed at the GdED's congress in Hamburg, the union demanded that the transport of nuclear waste to a nuclear storage facility in Gorleben be suspended until the German railway company Deutsche Bahn AG can guarantee the safety of workers and customers.</p>
<p>The chairman of the GdED, Rudi Schaefer, said he would be discussing this issue with the board of Deutsche Bahn later this week.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
